.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH skillastic 1  "skillastic 0.21.55" 
.SH NAME
skillastic \- Adaptive skill runtime: version\-aware skill lifecycle management for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskillastic\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-app\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skillastic — adaptive skill runtime.
.PP
Keeps AI\-agent skills compatible with the application they describe: deterministic version resolution, commit archaeology, context capture, and skill migration with lineage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-app\-version\fR \fI<SEMVER>\fR
Override the application version (semver) instead of auto\-detecting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skillastic\-init(1)
Initialize a .skillastic workspace in the current project
.TP
skillastic\-setup(1)
Configure this repo for the Skillastic skills (issue tracker, triage labels, domain docs)
.TP
skillastic\-add(1)
Register a new skill
.TP
skillastic\-remove(1)
Remove a skill
.TP
skillastic\-list(1)
List registered skills
.TP
skillastic\-show(1)
Show one skill in full
.TP
skillastic\-status(1)
Version\-resolver report for all skills vs. the current app version
.TP
skillastic\-archaeology(1)
Commit\-chain analysis between two app versions
.TP
skillastic\-capture(1)
Capture the current codebase context fingerprint
.TP
skillastic\-migrate(1)
Migrate a skill (or \-\-all) to the current app version
.TP
skillastic\-verify(1)
Mark a skill verified against the current app version
.TP
skillastic\-history(1)
Show a skill\*(Aqs lineage chain and mutation history
.TP
skillastic\-daemon(1)
Run the skillastic daemon (poll for app changes, auto\-resolve/migrate)
.TP
skillastic\-events(1)
Show recent daemon events recorded in the workspace state
.TP
skillastic\-audit(1)
Audit project roots for missing or incomplete .skillastic workspaces
.TP
skillastic\-promoted(1)
List and validate the promoted skill set
.TP
skillastic\-lint(1)
Lint the workspace and its skills
.TP
skillastic\-doctor(1)
Check workspace health and report actionable fixes
.TP
skillastic\-domain\-model(1)
Generate or update the project\*(Aqs CONTEXT.md domain glossary
.TP
skillastic\-adr(1)
Create a new architectural decision record
.TP
skillastic\-docs(1)
Generate or render human\-facing docs pages for skills
.TP
skillastic\-search(1)
Search registered skills by name, bucket, or body text
.TP
skillastic\-enroll(1)
First\-time setup: discover local repos, install the daemon, and make sure it survives logout/reboot
.TP
skillastic\-monitor(1)
Manage the multi\-repo daemon supervisor (used by the systemd unit `enroll` installs; rarely invoked directly)
.TP
skillastic\-register(1)
Create (or reuse) a .skillastic workspace for one or more projects and index them for daemon monitoring
.TP
skillastic\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.21.55
